 - **Preserve the current execution-profile representation.** In `mcp_servers[].tools`, each entry continues to mean the exact provider-native registered tool id exposed for that declared server. Do not add a new execution-profile schema merely to encode OMP naming. `core70.py` SHALL remove the Claude-only derivation that a server tool must spell `mcp__<server>__<tool>` and the global `startswith("mcp__")` inference. Instead it SHALL require: unique server names; exact stdio/server-id/entrypoint identity; no duplicate provider-native MCP tool id across declared servers; every declared server tool present exactly once in `native_tools`; every declared server/tool classified in the capability manifest; and the existing exact runtime native-tool/server-surface checks. An extra or missing runtime tool still fails closed even when its spelling does not identify its origin.
 - **OMP must separately prove the raw-server-tool to native-tool bijection.** The OMP adapter SHALL retain evidence that the six raw names returned by the frozen mediator `tools/list` correspond one-to-one with the six provider-native ids frozen in the OMP profile. The proof may use the exact OMP registry/catalog surface plus mediated calls and side-effect/object-version correlation; it may not rely only on a documented naming formula. The mediator executable digest, server id, OMP runtime/build, adapter/normalizer digest and exact native tool set make this binding part of the execution-profile evidence.
 - **Remove provider path ownership from the harness without creating an arbitrary hiding interface.** `harness70.py` SHALL obtain the installed protocol-package root from the adapter (for example as the return value of installation or a narrow accessor) and hash that exact root before and after execution; it SHALL not hard-code `.claude/skills`. Provider-specific control/runtime paths SHALL not be accepted as free-form oracle exclusions. Qualification-owned control/package state SHOULD live outside the workload project under run-owned state where the provider supports it. If a provider requires a project-local control path, it must be absent from the fixture baseline, created before launch, retained in the raw project-state record, bound by exact path/type/content or recursive digest before and after the run, and excluded from oracle diff/final-tree views only after the harness verifies the declared post-run policy. A provider may not hide an existing fixture path or an unverified subtree. Existing exact runtime-placeholder exclusion remains limited to paths whose reviewed identity/content is verified before exclusion.
